        { "id": "evt.hermes_confessed", "weight": 0.85,
          "text": "Hermes confessed: a woman arrived without a fare, facing a hundred years on the near shore. He folded foil taken from a newer grave and paid for her, then hid it. Charon was not angry about the money — about being made to break his rule without knowing. Minos recorded it as an irregularity rather than theft.",
